WEBVTT

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.818
Hmm. Kind of chilly.
有点冷

00:00:04.902 --> 00:00:07.321
(clears throat) Gentlemen,
here's what we know.
先生们，这是我们知道的

00:00:07.404 --> 00:00:11.325
Space rocks? Magnetic.
Asteroid? Also, magnetic.
宇宙石？有磁性，行星？也有磁性

00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:14.870
(gasps) Famed astrophysicist
Neil deBuck Weasel!
是著名的天文物理学家奈尔德巴克黄鼠狼

00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:16.330
He knows the cosmos.
他了解宇宙

00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:18.832
Ipso facto, thusly and ergo
根据事实来看，结果就是…

00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:20.876
the crash site must have
a heap of these things
撞击的地方
肯定有一堆这种吸引行星的东西

00:00:20.959 --> 00:00:22.795
attracting the asteroid.
撞击的地方
肯定有一堆这种吸引行星的东西

00:00:22.878 --> 00:00:25.506
Ooh. Pythagoras Buck.
He's got the right angle.
这是毕达哥拉斯巴克
他找到了正确的角度

00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:26.840
What if we use the magnets
如果我们用磁铁
把行星吸到别的地方呢？

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:28.509
to attract the asteroids somewhere else?
如果我们用磁铁
把行星吸到别的地方呢？

00:00:28.592 --> 00:00:30.344
As in, not towards Earth.
例如，不朝着地球来

00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:32.012
Theoretically speaking,
理论而言
如果把足够多的这玩意儿扔向宇宙…

00:00:32.096 --> 00:00:34.515
if we can launch
enough of these into space,
理论而言
如果把足够多的这玩意儿扔向宇宙…

00:00:34.598 --> 00:00:36.975
they will pull the asteroid off course.
就会把行星吸走了

00:00:38.102 --> 00:00:39.978
Thus, saving the world.
因此就拯救了世界

00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:41.313
(all cheering)

00:00:42.731 --> 00:00:44.858
So, we just need to go to the crash site
所以我们只需要去撞击点…

00:00:44.942 --> 00:00:47.361
and launch a bunch of rocks into space.
往宇宙中扔很多石头

00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:48.529
(chuckles) That's easy, right?
这简单，对吗？

00:00:48.612 --> 00:00:51.323
Oh, yeah. Sounds like a real piece of cake.
当然，听着真是小菜一碟

00:00:51.407 --> 00:00:52.991
This is progress!
这就是进展！

00:00:53.075 --> 00:00:55.327
Now we know exactly
what we don't know how to do.
现在我们明白了，只是不知道怎么去做

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.205
Vamanos, mammals!
走吧，哺乳动物们

00:00:58.288 --> 00:01:00.999
This trail will take us
directly to the crash site.
走这条路，直接就能到撞击点

00:01:03.794 --> 00:01:05.212
All right, kids.
好吧，孩子们

00:01:05.295 --> 00:01:07.089
(laughs) Let's have some fun.
我们来点乐子

00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:09.049
-(laughs)
-Oh!

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.342
(whimpers)
好吧，各位，沿着小路走

00:01:10.426 --> 00:01:12.553
Okay, everyone. Follow the trail.
好吧，各位，沿着小路走

00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:14.680
Never leave the trail.
不要离开这条路

00:01:14.763 --> 00:01:16.807
-(distant screeching)
-Hmm?

00:01:19.476 --> 00:01:20.477
(gasps)

00:01:22.688 --> 00:01:24.732
Okay, everyone. Leave the trail.
好吧，各位，离开这条路

00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:26.400
Into the forest. Chop, chop.
进森林，快

00:01:26.483 --> 00:01:28.444
-But you just said...
-(stammers)
可你刚说…

00:01:28.527 --> 00:01:31.113
You know I'm crazy. Come on.
我是个疯子，拜托

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:36.869
(roaring)

00:01:37.536 --> 00:01:38.537
(grunts)

00:01:40.956 --> 00:01:42.249
(Buck screams)

00:01:42.332 --> 00:01:43.584
(all gasp)

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.003
(clears throat)
I love the shade. Don't you?
我喜欢阴凉，你呢？

00:01:46.795 --> 00:01:48.422
Well played, weasel.
干得漂亮，黄鼠狼

00:01:48.505 --> 00:01:49.757
Stay sharp, kids.
保持警惕，孩子们

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.800
They can't hide forever.
他们不可能总躲着

00:02:03.687 --> 00:02:04.772
DIEGO: Hey, Buck.
嘿，巴克

00:02:04.855 --> 00:02:07.441
You have a suggestion
for getting around the river?
你有过河的办法吗？

00:02:07.524 --> 00:02:10.694
Let's see if the tablet's
ancient wisdom will guide us.
来看看碑上面古人的智慧能不能指引我们

00:02:11.028 --> 00:02:12.029
Hmm.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.031
Hmm.

00:02:20.078 --> 00:02:21.079
(grunting)

00:02:23.874 --> 00:02:24.875
(laughs)

00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:28.504
(alarm blaring)

00:02:29.004 --> 00:02:30.380
(screams)

00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:32.049
(grunts)

00:02:36.011 --> 00:02:38.597
(echoing) Let my mammals pass!
让我的哺乳动物过去！

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.265
That's never gonna work.
那不可能有用的

00:02:47.439 --> 00:02:50.484
The ancients grant us safe passage.
古人赋予我们安全的通道

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.611
(chuckles) Sweet!
厉害！

00:02:56.907 --> 00:02:57.908
(grunts)

00:03:01.578 --> 00:03:02.579
(screams)

00:03:17.719 --> 00:03:20.138
Wow, the air feels strange.
喔，空气有点怪

00:03:20.597 --> 00:03:22.015
-(electricity crackling)
-Uh...
迭戈？

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:23.267
Diego?
迭戈？

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:25.561
Hmm...

00:03:26.144 --> 00:03:28.313
(snickering)
怎么了？

00:03:28.397 --> 00:03:29.523
What?
怎么了？

00:03:29.606 --> 00:03:30.941
(Sid and Diego laughing)

00:03:33.944 --> 00:03:34.987
(grunts)

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.488
(laughing)

00:03:36.572 --> 00:03:38.282
(screams and grunts)

00:03:40.117 --> 00:03:41.618
(both laughing)

00:03:42.077 --> 00:03:43.662
(both grunting)
总算有了！我们有超能力了！

00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:47.040
Finally! We have superpowers!
总算有了！我们有超能力了！

00:03:47.124 --> 00:03:48.750
(both exclaiming)

00:03:50.419 --> 00:03:51.587
Ladies and gentlemen,
女士们先生们，我们走进了雷暴

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:54.548
we have wandered into an electrical storm.
女士们先生们，我们走进了雷暴

00:03:54.631 --> 00:03:55.674
(thunder rumbling)
我建议大家离树远点儿

00:03:55.757 --> 00:03:58.302
I suggest we all stay away from the trees.
我建议大家离树远点儿

00:03:58.969 --> 00:04:00.053
Sure, no problem.
当然，没问题，感觉不像在森林里

00:04:00.137 --> 00:04:01.513
It's not like we're in a forest.
当然，没问题，感觉不像在森林里

00:04:01.597 --> 00:04:03.557
(both exclaiming)

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.975
(thunder rumbling)

00:04:07.019 --> 00:04:10.230
Boy, Mother Nature sure
is in a bad mood lately.
没想到啊，自然母亲近来闹脾气了

00:04:10.314 --> 00:04:12.858
Good thing we're all here to help each other.
好的一点是，我们都在互相扶持

00:04:12.941 --> 00:04:16.278
Oh, like I always say, stay close, stay alive.
正如我常说的，离近一点，活得好

00:04:16.361 --> 00:04:17.863
-(thunder cracks)
-(gasps)

00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:23.869
There they are!
他们在那！

00:04:23.952 --> 00:04:26.455
Right out in the open. (laughs)
在一块露天的地方

00:04:26.538 --> 00:04:28.248
How stupid can you be?
你怎么能这么笨呢？

00:04:28.332 --> 00:04:30.500
Come on, kids. Dive!
来吧，孩子们，俯冲！

00:04:36.882 --> 00:04:40.761
Everyone, try not to create
any sort of friction.
各位，尽可能别产生摩擦

00:04:40.844 --> 00:04:42.763
No friction. Got it.
别产生摩擦，明白

00:04:42.846 --> 00:04:44.723
Yup. Cool beans.
对，明白

00:04:44.806 --> 00:04:46.475
Friction is what now?
摩擦会怎么样？

00:04:47.726 --> 00:04:49.144
Oh, no.
哦，不

00:04:53.482 --> 00:04:55.359
(all screaming)

00:04:56.401 --> 00:04:57.903
(yelping)

00:04:58.904 --> 00:05:00.697
Come on! Let's get out of here.
快！我们离开这

00:05:02.282 --> 00:05:03.283
(Sid screams)

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.701
(both scream)

00:05:08.038 --> 00:05:10.624
-Hurry, Granny.
-Don't you hurry me.
–快点，奶奶
–别催我

00:05:10.707 --> 00:05:13.168
I've been struck by lightning more times...
我被闪电打中过很多次…

00:05:13.251 --> 00:05:14.586
Ahh! Granny!
奶奶！

00:05:15.045 --> 00:05:17.047
...than you've had hot breakfasts.
比你吃过的热乎乎的早饭的次数还多

00:05:18.882 --> 00:05:20.008
-(grunting)
-(gasping)

00:05:21.093 --> 00:05:23.011
-(grunts)
-Peaches!
桃子！

00:05:24.179 --> 00:05:25.347
(screams)
朱利安，别动！

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.599
Julian, don't move!
朱利安，别动！

00:05:27.683 --> 00:05:28.684
Oh!

00:05:30.268 --> 00:05:31.561
I have an idea.
我有办法了

00:05:32.187 --> 00:05:34.147
-(gasps)
-I'm coming, sweetheart!
我来了，宝贝！

00:05:35.023 --> 00:05:36.775
Julian, why aren't you helping her?
–朱利安，你干吗不救她？
–等等！不，曼尼，她…

00:05:36.858 --> 00:05:38.819
-Wait! No, Manny, she...
-(both scream)
–朱利安，你干吗不救她？
–等等！不，曼尼，她…

00:05:38.902 --> 00:05:39.903
(grunts)

00:05:43.198 --> 00:05:44.783
Uh, what are you guys doing?
你们在干什么？

00:05:44.866 --> 00:05:45.993
Helping?
帮忙？

00:05:46.076 --> 00:05:47.744
What would "not helping" look like?
“不帮忙”会怎么样？

00:05:49.204 --> 00:05:51.748
-Hey, zapheads!
-Whoo!
嘿，摩擦傻蛋！

00:05:52.124 --> 00:05:53.125
(both grunting)

00:05:55.043 --> 00:05:57.087
(both screaming)

00:05:58.046 --> 00:06:00.090
Manny, get ready to run.
曼尼，准备跑

00:06:01.883 --> 00:06:03.552
Come on, let's go!
快，我们走！

00:06:05.804 --> 00:06:07.431
-(grunts)
-(both continue screaming)

00:06:10.475 --> 00:06:11.476
(all screaming)

00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:16.648
Everybody make it?
大家都出来了？

00:06:16.732 --> 00:06:18.734
Shira, Manny, Crash, Eddie, Ellie, Granny.
希拉、曼尼、喀什、艾迪、埃丽、奶奶

00:06:18.817 --> 00:06:20.736
Aw, shoot! I'm out of fingers.
啊，讨厌！手指头不够用了

00:06:20.819 --> 00:06:22.487
Buck. Where's Buck?
巴克，巴克呢？

00:06:25.282 --> 00:06:26.324
Do you hear that?
你听到了吗？

00:06:28.076 --> 00:06:29.161
A baby!
一个宝宝！

00:06:29.244 --> 00:06:31.079
There's a baby in there!
里面有个宝宝！

00:06:31.455 --> 00:06:33.790
Buck, wait! It's too dangerous.
巴克，等等！太危险了

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.713
(both gasp)
他死了

00:06:39.796 --> 00:06:41.173
He's gone.
他死了

00:06:41.256 --> 00:06:42.883
I can't believe it.
我不相信

00:06:42.966 --> 00:06:45.802
Don't know how we'll
go on without you, Buck.
没有你我们怎么办，巴克

00:06:46.595 --> 00:06:48.388
All right, let's go.
好吧，我们走

00:06:48.472 --> 00:06:49.473
(Buck screaming)

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.808
It's Buck!
是巴克！

00:06:53.018 --> 00:06:55.479
(groaning)

00:06:56.521 --> 00:06:57.981
(grunts) Huh?

00:06:58.482 --> 00:07:01.401
I got you. Don't worry, I got you.
有我在，别担心，我在

00:07:01.485 --> 00:07:03.695
There you are. There.
没事了，没事

00:07:03.779 --> 00:07:06.114
-Say, "hi," everyone.
-ALL: Huh?
大家，打个招呼啊

00:07:06.823 --> 00:07:08.742
Isn't she gorgeous?
“她”漂亮不？

00:07:08.825 --> 00:07:10.619
How can he tell it's a she?
他为什么说“她”？

00:07:11.661 --> 00:07:12.746
Oh.
多乖的小家伙

00:07:12.829 --> 00:07:15.123
Such a good little poochie-woochie.
多乖的小家伙

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:19.669
(chuckles) Just to be clear,
that's a pumpkin, right?
我就确认一下，那是个南瓜，对吗？

00:07:20.337 --> 00:07:23.548
She has a little jaundice,
but I think she'll be okay.
“她”得了黄疸，可我觉得“她”没事

00:07:23.632 --> 00:07:25.467
Yes, you will.
是啊，没错

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:29.304
I think I'll call you... Bronwyn.
我想我要叫你…布朗纹

00:07:29.721 --> 00:07:32.099
Um, little buddy? We need you
back on planet Earth.
朋友？你得正常回来

00:07:32.182 --> 00:07:34.476
While it's still here. Okay?
问题还没解决呢，好吗？

00:07:34.559 --> 00:07:35.811
Right you are, mammal.
你说得对，哺乳动物

00:07:35.894 --> 00:07:39.356
Who wants to save the world
from the fiery asteroid?
有人想拯救地球
免于受到火热的行星撞击吗？

00:07:39.439 --> 00:07:40.440
-(sniffing)
-You do!
你想！

00:07:42.359 --> 00:07:43.318
Hmm.

00:07:43.401 --> 00:07:44.402
(sniffing)

